/Title <653230307A3420506F77657220417263686974656374757265209220436F7265202D205265666572656E6365204D616E75614C>
/Author (Freescale Semiconductor; Inc.)
/ModDate (D:20120920122133-05'00')
/Subject (Supports e200z446n3. The primary objective of this manual is to describe the functionality of the e200z4 embedded microprocessor core for software and hardware developers. The e200z4 processor family is a set of CPU cores that implement low-cost versions of Power Architecture technology. The e200z4 core is a dual-issue, 32-bit design with 64-bit general-purpose registers \(GPRs\).)
/Keywords ("e200z4, Power Architecture, Power Architecture, general-purpose registers \(GPRs\), e200z446n3")
